Localized Thermal Processing Supports Advanced Chips

Laser annealing applies optical energy to selected wafer regions for very short periods. This enables manufacturers to activate implanted dopants, form contacts and modify materials while reducing heat diffusion into temperature-sensitive structures.

These capabilities are increasingly relevant as device dimensions shrink and process requirements become more demanding.

Logic, Memory and Power Semiconductors Drive Adoption

